{
 "_doc": [
  "The replay corpus: the 10 archived designs and, per design, the cad runs tools/verify_all.sh makes on it (same configs,",
  "overlays, --only sets and CAD_LAYER_CHECK), so a verify_all scratch dir can be scored without re-running Blender",
  "(replay.py --from-verify DIR; verify_out is the file name verify_all writes under its run dir).",
  "kind 'designer': what the designer's own config and the always-on tools report (what an agent sees at hand-off).",
  "kind 'review': the same model with the rows each reviewer showed were missing (overlays), so it measures a check given the row.",
  "Runs with no verify_out are bench-only (verify_all has no pure designer run on v2 A1: it always adds R1's overlays).",
  "{dir} in args is the attempt's example directory."
 ],
 "attempts": {
